Name: libsmb2
Summary: SMB2/3 client library
Vendor: Ronnie Sahlberg
Packager: ronniesahlberg@gmail.com
Version: @VERSION@
Release: 1
Epoch: 0
License: GNU LGPL version 2.1
Group: System Environment/Libraries
URL: http://www.github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2

Source: libsmb2-%{version}.tar.gz

Provides: lib = %{version}

BuildRequires: gcc, make, autoconf, automake, libtool
BuildRequires: krb5-devel

Prefix: /usr
BuildRoot: %{_tmppath}/%{name}-%{version}-root

%description
Libsmb2 is a SMB2/3 client library.

This package also contains the smb2-ls and smb2-cp utilities.

#######################################################################



%prep
%setup -q
# setup the init script and sysconfig file
%setup -T -D -n libsmb2-%{version} -q

%build

## check for ccache
if ccache -h >/dev/null 2>&1 ; then
	CC="ccache gcc"
else
	CC="gcc"
fi

export CC

## always run autogen.sh
aclocal
autoheader
autoconf
libtoolize -c -f -i
automake --add-missing


CFLAGS="$RPM_OPT_FLAGS $EXTRA -O2 -D_GNU_SOURCE" %configure --disable-libdcerpc
make %{?_smp_mflags}

%install
# Clean up in case there is trash left from a previous build
rm -rf $RPM_BUILD_ROOT

# Create the target build directory hierarchy

make DESTDIR=$RPM_BUILD_ROOT install

# Remove "*.old" files
find $RPM_BUILD_ROOT -name "*.old" -exec rm -f {} \;

# Do not ship libtool archives
find $RPM_BUILD_ROOT -name "*.la" -exec rm -f {} \;

%clean
rm -rf $RPM_BUILD_ROOT


#######################################################################
## Files section                                                     ##
#######################################################################

%files
%defattr(-,root,root)

%{_libdir}/libsmb2.so.*
%{_bindir}/smb2-cp
%{_bindir}/smb2-ls

%package devel
Summary: Development libraries for LibSMB2
Group: Development
Requires: %{name} = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}

%description devel
development libraries for LibSMB2

%files devel
%defattr(-,root,root)
%{_includedir}/smb2/libsmb2.h
%{_includedir}/smb2/libsmb2-share-enum.h
%{_includedir}/smb2/libsmb2-raw.h
%{_includedir}/smb2/smb2.h
%{_includedir}/smb2/smb2-errors.h
%{_libdir}/libsmb2.so
%{_libdir}/libsmb2.a
%{_libdir}/pkgconfig/libsmb2.pc

%changelog
* Thu Nov 19 2026 : Version 7.0.0
 - New soname 7. Full DCE/RPC moved out to the separate libdcerpc
   library; libsmb2 keeps a small flat smb2_share_enum_*() API.
 - SMB2 over QUIC ("quic" URL argument) and over SMB Direct ("rdma"),
   Linux only, built in when libquic or rdma-core is found.
 - IAKerb authentication (sec=iakerb).
 - Optional OpenSSL 3 libcrypto: AES-128-GCM and AES-256-GCM for
   SMB 3.1.1, and signing and sealing through OpenSSL.
 - AES-CMAC signing with AES-NI over the iovecs, without a copy.
 - smb2_symlink(), smb2_link(), server-side copy (FSCTL_SRV_COPYCHUNK),
   setting security descriptors, change notify, SMB2 CANCEL, unrelated
   compound requests and the *_async_pdu() calls.
 - smb2_set_seal() takes NONE/MAYBE/MUST, and sealed replies are
   enforced when sealing is required.
 - Server: encrypted sessions, SMB 3.1.1 cipher negotiation, Kerberos
   and IAKerb, SMB over QUIC, oplock and lease breaks, every directory
   information class, getters for the current request's tree id and
   async id, and many fixes from embedded servers (issues #474, #500).
 - Bounds checks throughout the PDU, NTLMSSP, SPNEGO and share
   enumeration decoders, including all fixes in 6.3.0 to 6.3.2.
 - Contexts used on different threads no longer share any state.
 - New platforms and fixes: Haiku, the PS2 IOP (smb2man.irx),
   GameCube/Wii, macOS.
* Tue Nov 03 2026 : Version 6.3.2
 - Security fixes for malformed or hostile server replies:
   CVE-2026-110713: bound the volume label and filesystem name
   lengths in FS_VOLUME/FS_ATTRIBUTE info replies (heap over-read).
   CVE-2026-110714: reject ACL sizes and descriptor offsets that
   underflow or wrap in security descriptors (heap over-read).
   A malformed SID inside an ACE now fails decoding instead of
   leaving a NULL sid behind.
 - Build fix for -Werror with newer glibc.
* Sun Oct 25 2026 : Version 6.3.1
 - Security fix for a malformed or hostile server reply:
   a directory entry that fails to decode no longer leaves two
   entries owning the same name (double free), and a wrapping
   NextEntryOffset no longer loops until memory runs out.
* Thu Oct 22 2026 : Version 6.3.0
 - Security fixes for malformed or hostile server replies:
   bounds checks on lengths and offsets in the PDU, NTLMSSP and
   SPNEGO decoders, the FILE_ALL_INFORMATION name, header-only
   replies, QUERY_INFO replies without data and the DCE/RPC
   array and string counts used by share enumeration.
* Mon Dec 16 2024 : Version 6.1.0
 - Fix return code for smb2-ls on failure
 - Fix memory errors in smb2_opendir()
 - Add a macro te test for the version of the share-enum api
* Wed Dec 11 2024 : Version 6.0.0
 - Major rewrites to DCE-RPC
 - Initial support for building servers
* Mon Jan 17 2022 : Version 4.0.0
 - Add support for SMB3 encryption
 - Add support for Anonymous NTLMSSP logins
 - Add support for readlink.
 - Add API to notify application of changes to which filehandles are used by
 libsmb2.
 - Add support for Big Endian DCERPC and allow it to be controlled from the
 URL.
 - Add support for 3.1.1 signing
 - Add support for PS2(EE) and PS3
 - Fixes to UCS2 when compose characters are used.
 
 - Various MacOS fixes
 - Fix a few NULL dereferences
* Mon Jun 10 2019 : Version 3.0.0
 - ESP32 support
 - Support specifying the port number in an SMB URL.
 - Add creation time to smb_stat
 - Abort all commands when the context is destroyed.
 - Free all file and directory handles when the context is destroyed.
 - Fix handling of O_TRUNC
 - Add more error codes.
 - Add support for SMB2_IOCTL
 - Handle DCE/RPC fragment reassembly for IOCTL().
* Sat Jul 7 2018 : Version 2.0.0
 - SMB2/3 signing
 - Kerberos authentication
 - Builtin NTLMSSP authentication for when libkrb5 is not available
 - Share enumeration
 - CMake support
 - Various bugfixes
* Sun Mar 5 2017 : Version 1.0.0
 - Initial version
